---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TesseractHero from '../components/TesseractHero.astro';
import HeroCanvas from '../components/HeroCanvas.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Parametric CAD from sketch to shop floor" description="Chudware is a parametric CAD system for mechanical engineers: exact solid geometry, an editable feature tree, assemblies, CAM, PLM, and simulation, in a browser or as a native Windows, Linux, and macOS desktop application.">
  <TesseractHero>
    <p class="eyebrow">Parametric CAD · Browser or native</p>
    <h1>Parametric CAD, <span class="text-gradient">from sketch to shop floor.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Chudware is built for mechanical engineers and product teams who want modeling, assemblies, CAM, PLM, simulation, reverse engineering, and an AI copilot in the same workspace.</p>
    <p class="hero-note">In a browser you get the real application, not a video stream of a machine in a data centre. Signed native builds for Windows, Linux, and macOS are ready to download.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/product/">Tour the product</a>
    </div>
    <dl class="architecture-strip" slot="strip" aria-label="Chudware at a glance">
      <div><dt>Geometry</dt><dd>Exact B-rep solids, not meshes</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Interoperability</dt><dd>STEP, IGES, and BREP in and out</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Isolation</dt><dd>Per-account roots at the gateway</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Native</dt><dd>Windows, Linux, macOS</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </TesseractHero>

  <section class="capability-index" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" id="capabilities-title">The engineering loop</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Parametric modeling</li>
        <li>Constraint sketching</li>
        <li>Assemblies</li>
        <li>CAM</li>
        <li>Simulation</li>
        <li>Reverse engineering</li>
        <li>PLM</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="architecture">
    <div class="wrap architecture-layout">
      <header class="section-heading architecture-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">The real application, in a tab</p>
        <h2>Full CAD in a browser tab, without turning CAD into a web toy.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The browser runs the same application as the desktop build. Model state and tool calls go over the wire — never a video stream of a machine in a data centre — so the geometry kernel and the full engineering toolchain stay intact instead of being reduced to fit a web page.</p>
        <p class="supporting-copy">Prefer local execution? <a class="text-link" href="/download/">Native builds for Windows, Linux, and macOS</a> run the same product surface on an engineering workstation.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="pricing-note">
        <p class="eyebrow">Open a supplier's file, not only your own</p>
        <p>Chudware opens STEP, IGES, and BREP solids, STL, OBJ, PLY, and glTF meshes, and DXF for 2D profiles. It writes STEP, IGES, BREP, STL, OBJ, PLY, and glTF back out.</p>
        <p>The native <code>.step+</code> document is a container: a neutral STEP body stored alongside the parametric tree. Any CAD system can open the STEP inside it, so an editable design is never trapped in a format only Chudware can read.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <HeroCanvas>
    <p class="eyebrow">Live from the feature tree</p>
    <h2>A parametric rebuild, replayed in front of you.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Every Chudware model is an ordered feature history — sketches, extrusions, fillets, holes — that can be edited and rebuilt deterministically. Watch one re-execute: the same operation stream the FeatureManager drives in the product, rendered here as an exact boolean field.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/product/modeling/">How modeling works</a></div>
  </HeroCanvas>

  <section class="section workbench-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">One project, not a relay race</p>
        <h2>Keep design intent attached as the work moves downstream.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The feature tree, manufacturing plan, product data, artifacts, and copilot activity live in one engineering environment instead of being handed between disconnected tools.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="workbench">
        <figure class="workbench-image">
          <img src="/images/cam.png" width="1340" height="838" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware manufacturing workspace showing a CAM job, stock, tools, operations, and toolpath simulation" />
          <figcaption>Captured from Chudware's real manufacturing workspace.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <ol class="workflow-list">
          <li><span><Icon name="overview" /></span><div><h3>Model with intent</h3><p>Constrained sketches and ordered features keep dimensions, references, and revisions explicit.</p></div></li>
          <li><span><Icon name="package" /></span><div><h3>Carry geometry into production</h3><p>Build CAM operations and inspect simulation alongside the source design.</p></div></li>
          <li><span><Icon name="archive" /></span><div><h3>Trace the product</h3><p>PLM connects project history and artifacts to the engineering work that produced them.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section copilot-section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI that operates the tools</p>
        <h2>The copilot works inside the model, not in a disconnected chat window.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Describe the engineering intent in plain language. The copilot drives Chudware's modeling tools, and the result remains a normal, inspectable model with sketches and features.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/ai-copilot/">Read the copilot guide</a></div>
      </header>
      <ol class="tool-loop" aria-label="Copilot modeling loop">
        <li><span>Intent</span><strong>Describe the part and its constraints</strong></li>
        <li><span>Context</span><strong>Work against the open model</strong></li>
        <li><span>Tools</span><strong>Drive the same modeling operations</strong></li>
        <li><span>Result</span><strong>Inspect sketches, features, and geometry</strong></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section source-section">
    <div class="wrap source-band">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Verify before you cut metal</p><h2>Analysis attached to the model that produced it.</h2></div>
      <p>Run linear static stress, modal, and thermal studies against the same feature tree you modeled, with error-driven adaptive mesh refinement and a second, independent mesher available to check whether a result is a property of the part or of the mesh.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/product/simulation/">How simulation works <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="chudcode-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">In development · Companion product</p>
        <h2 id="chudcode-title">Meet Chudcode, our workspace for software work.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Chudcode brings repository context, agent tools, sessions, review, debugging, and version history into one focused desktop environment. It is early, deliberately separate from the CAD product, and being built in public-facing stages.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/chudcode/">See what we’re building</a></div>
      </header>
      <div class="pricing-note">
        <p class="eyebrow">Free desktop distribution</p>
        <p>Chudcode is still a major work in progress. When public desktop builds are ready, the binaries will be free to download—no Chudware subscription or browser workspace required.</p>
        <ul class="fact-list">
          <li>Agent-guided coding with real repository context</li>
          <li>Integrated tools, review, debugging, and history</li>
          <li>A focused teaser product; Chudware remains the flagship</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start in the browser</p>
      <h2>Open a full engineering workspace from a tab.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Create an account for browser access, or download the desktop app for Windows, Linux, or macOS.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/download/">Download the desktop app</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
